      "expected_observable_result": "Cloud Desktop renders and updates the authenticated global user profile through Cloud authority. Local Desktop renders the same native read-only identity projection through sidecar auth-me and returns a stable unavailable state for mutation; neither mode caches secret credentials or falls back to Web UI. Until the observed authority carries a current revision, Snapshot v4 keeps both surfaces unavailable at the capability gate.",
      "judgment_rationale": "UserProfile owns two tenant-nested production route registrations, but its authority is the global authenticated user. The page reads useAuthStore.user; authAPI.login and authAPI.verifyToken hydrate that store through GET /auth/me, while profile and language mutations use PUT /users/me and password change uses POST /auth/force-change-password. Desktop now binds profileRouteClient, profileRouteController, profileRouteModule, ProfileRoutePage, and the auxiliary deep-link host through App and SettingsWindow. The observed Cloud client exposes all four actions, and the observed Local client exposes read-only auth-me with local_profile_mutation_authority_unavailable for mutation. Both P2 projections still publish authority_revision null, so Snapshot v4 fails both surfaces closed to capability_authority_revision_unavailable rather than promoting the native route from source declarations alone."
